<title>UK: U.K. reserves fell underlying $93 mln in April.</title>
<headline>U.K. reserves fell underlying $93 mln in April.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's gold and currency reserves fell an underlying $93.0 million in April, the Treasury said.</p>
<p>(IN MLN DOLLARS EXCEPT WHERE STATED)</p>
<p>					April		  March</p>
<p> Underlying reserves change   - 93		    - 98</p>
<p> Change in actual reserves    +552		    - 105</p>
<p> Total actual reserves	  40.61 billion	40.06 billion</p>
<p>The underlying change excludes factors included in the total change</p>
<p>- Repayments under the</p>
<p>- exchange cover scheme (ECS) of $88 million</p>
<p>- Revaluation arising from EMI swap of $237 million</p>
<p>- Government debt assigned from public sector $75 million</p>
<p>- ECU T-bills maturing exceeded those issued by $1 million</p>
<p>- ECU T-note issue of $571 million</p>
<p>London Forex desk +44-171-542-6284</p>
</text>
